          "text": "## Best structure solution\n\nThe pattern indexes as an **orthorhombic primitive cell**, with systematic absences consistent with **Pnma (No. 62)**. The derived cell is approximately:\n\n\\[\na=8.895\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=3.520\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=4.968\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad Z=4.\n\\]\n\nRepresentative indexing is 19.95\u00b0 (200), 31.12\u00b0 (011), 32.39\u00b0 (210), 36.13\u00b0 (002), 41.61\u00b0 (202), 44.54\u00b0 (401), and 49.2\u201349.3\u00b0 (212). The split high-angle envelopes are accounted for by overlapping orthorhombic reflections.\n\nThe V sublattice and space group are well determined. Because Li scatters weakly with Cu X-rays, its position and the F coordinates should be regarded as a chemically restrained powder solution suitable for final Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_LiVF4_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder indexing and chemically restrained structure solution'\n_chemical_name_common                 'lithium vanadium(III) fluoride'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'LiVF4'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Li1 V1 F4'\n_chemical_formula_weight              133.88\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 4\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe               x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_type                'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n\n_space_group_crystal_system           orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number                62\n\n_cell_length_a                        8.895\n_cell_length_b                        3.520\n_cell_length_c                        4.968\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          155.56\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_